  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "Suppose that \\(z\\) is any complex number which is not equal to any of \\(\\{3,3\\omega,3\\omega^2\\}\\) where \\(\\omega\\) is a complex cube root of unity. Then \\(\\displaystyle\\frac1{z-3}+\\frac1{z-3\\omega}+\\frac1{z-3\\omega^2}\\) equals",
  "options": {
    "A": "\\(\\frac{3z^2+3z}{(z-3)^3}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\frac{3z^2+3\\omega z}{z^3-27}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\frac{3z^2}{z^3-3z^2+9z-27}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\frac{3z^2}{z^3-27}\\)"
  },
  "answer": "D",
